# Scoped to source/daemon/Dockerfile.test only. BuildKit picks up
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore alongside the Dockerfile and uses it in
# preference to any context-root .dockerignore.
#
# The test Dockerfile compiles the Rust workspace from local sources,
# embeds the three frontend dist/ trees via rust-embed, and runs
# deploy/install.sh against a synthetic release bundle. Everything else
# in the repo is noise — exclude build artefacts, IDE state, and
# unrelated workspaces to keep the build context small and avoid cache
# invalidation when files outside the daemon scope change.

# Default-deny, then allow the trees the Dockerfile copies.
*

!source/daemon/
# Real frontend dist/ + admin-site's include'd logo asset, copied only
# by the WEB_DIST=real path (web-real stage) for the Playwright UI
# suite. Harmless for the default placeholder build, which never reads
# them. Populate with `make build-web` before a WEB_DIST=real build.
!source/admin-site/dist/
!source/admin-site/src/assets/
!source/user-app/dist/
!source/admin-app/dist/
!deploy/
# Public-facing release version. The daemon's build scripts read it
# at compile time via build-support/version.rs::read_calver.
!CALVER

# Re-deny build artefacts inside the allowed trees. These are large
# (Rust target/, node_modules/) and bust the build cache on every
# touch even when the Dockerfile inputs haven't changed.
source/daemon/target/
source/daemon/.target-linux/
source/daemon/fuzz/target/
source/daemon/fuzz/corpus/
source/daemon/fuzz/artifacts/
**/node_modules/
**/.DS_Store
.git/
.target-linux/
